<title>NICARAGUA: Nicaraguan president departs for Spain.</title>
<headline>Nicaraguan president departs for Spain.</headline>
<dateline>MANAGUA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nicaraguan President Arnoldo Aleman on Thursday left for Barcelona to attend the Interamerican Development Bank's annual meeting, saying he would ask the bankers to maintain foreign aid to Nicaragua.</p>
<p>While in Spain for the meetings Monday and Tuesday, Aleman, a right-wing lawyer and coffee grower who took power on January 10, will meet with Spanish President Jose Maria Aznar to discuss Spanish aid to Nicaragua, a government press release said.</p>
<p>No date was specified for the meeting.</p>
</text>
